WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.115
Risk informs where the design review needs
depth.

2
00:00:03.235 --> 00:00:06.179
In our fictional case, a missing mixing
protection

3
00:00:06.299 --> 00:00:09.392
can permit transfer after loss of
agitation,

4
00:00:09.512 --> 00:00:12.541
potentially affecting concentration
uniformity.

5
00:00:12.661 --> 00:00:16.011
Explain that mechanism before assigning a
priority.

6
00:00:16.131 --> 00:00:19.437
Another issue, such as an inconsistent
drawing title,

7
00:00:19.557 --> 00:00:22.075
may primarily affect document control.

8
00:00:22.195 --> 00:00:25.501
Both require action, but their
consequences differ.

9
00:00:25.621 --> 00:00:29.099
A risk label without an explanation gives
the reviewer

10
00:00:29.219 --> 00:00:32.397
little basis for deciding what evidence is
enough.

11
00:00:33.017 --> 00:00:36.089
A numerical risk score can organize
discussion

12
00:00:36.209 --> 00:00:38.327
but cannot supply missing knowledge.

13
00:00:38.447 --> 00:00:41.796
This lesson uses no universal score
threshold.

14
00:00:41.916 --> 00:00:46.162
If a serious failure has weak evidence for
prevention or detection,

15
00:00:46.282 --> 00:00:48.543
keep that uncertainty visible even

16
00:00:48.663 --> 00:00:50.839
when an arithmetic total looks small.

17
00:00:50.959 --> 00:00:54.714
Review assumptions, operating conditions
and dependencies.

18
00:00:54.834 --> 00:00:56.925
Do not reduce a risk rating merely

19
00:00:57.045 --> 00:00:59.986
because a proposed control appears on the
drawing;

20
00:01:00.106 --> 00:01:03.818
its effectiveness still needs support and
later verification.

21
00:01:04.438 --> 00:01:08.363
For the mixing scenario, the proposed
control inhibits transfer

22
00:01:08.483 --> 00:01:10.958
when loss of agitation is detected.

23
00:01:11.078 --> 00:01:13.382
Review sensor coverage, logic,

24
00:01:13.502 --> 00:01:16.105
bypass authority and reset behaviour.

25
00:01:16.225 --> 00:01:20.695
Ask whether the sensing arrangement could
miss the failure being considered.

26
00:01:20.815 --> 00:01:22.992
Link the design response to a planned

27
00:01:23.112 --> 00:01:25.935
controlled challenge of the protective
function.

28
00:01:26.055 --> 00:01:28.679
The teaching diagram shows failure,
control

29
00:01:28.799 --> 00:01:31.359
and verification as connected steps,

30
00:01:31.479 --> 00:01:35.298
not as proof that any specific interlock
is already effective.

31
00:01:35.918 --> 00:01:39.843
A useful risk-informed review records what
remains uncertain,

32
00:01:39.963 --> 00:01:43.493
who will resolve it and what change
triggers another review.

33
00:01:43.613 --> 00:01:46.791
For example, a later product with
different viscosity

34
00:01:46.911 --> 00:01:49.770
may invalidate the original mixing
assumption.

35
00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:53.184
Keep that trigger linked to the
requirements and design.

36
00:01:53.304 --> 00:01:56.419
Your activity is to compare two design
findings

37
00:01:56.539 --> 00:01:59.056
and justify the depth of review for each.

38
00:01:59.176 --> 00:02:02.782
Do not force every question into a
numerical ranking

39
00:02:02.902 --> 00:02:05.196
when a reasoned explanation is clearer.
